fact WorkItem(id: "WI-582", description: some(value: "WI-502 typed rule pattern SYNTAX — the explicit ?x: T binder (new grammar), distinct from the implicit requires path (WI-292). Add the EXPLICIT surface for typed rule patterns per docs/design/constrained-term-substrate.md §\"Typed rule patterns — surface and matching\": a type-variable introducer [E] on a rule head (operation conventions — rule add[T](?x: T, 0) = ?x :- Numeric[T]) and a : T annotation on a pattern variable in a rule LHS (inline rule add(?x: Numeric, 0) = ?x). SEMANTICS (desugaring): head(…, ?x: T, …) :- body MEANS head(…, ?x, …) :- conforms(typeof(?x), T), body — conforms = subsort (sort bound) / provides (spec bound), an ordinary SLD goal over the carried type. REALIZATION: the loader installs the bound as a Type(T) CONSTRAINT on the rule variable (the Step-1 store, WI-570), keyed by the DeBruijn index on the rule template and opened to the fresh VarId at with_fresh_vars; matching then rides the EXISTING Step-2 bind_waking (WI-571) + the carried type (WI-578) — the SAME wakeup the implicit path (WI-292) wires, so NO new matcher. A type-variable bound is declared ONCE: a non-linear p[T](?x: T, ?x) shares one T across both occurrences (must bind alike AND type alike); a conflicting re-annotation is a LOUD load error. The body-guard form (conforms(typeof(?x), T) as an explicit goal) is the equivalent fallback for a bound spanning several variables. SCOPE: grammar.js ([T] type-params after a rule-head functor + : Type on a rule-LHS pattern var — remember the WI-517 gotcha: a parenthesized single typed binder must be a NAMED node, pattern_typed) + lowering + loader Type-constraint installation. Reuses the dormant Pattern::Var.type_ann channel (WI-318 created it, WI-517 used it for lambda binders — prior art). NOT in scope: the implicit requires firing (WI-292) and the typed-value carrier (WI-578); this CONSUMES both. PRODUCER of new rule-head/goal functor symbols -> MUST honor the WI-581 canonicalization guardrail (canonical resolved symbol, never a fresh/short/unique intern). ACCEPTANCE: rule add[T](?x: T, 0) = ?x :- Numeric[T] and the inline rule add(?x: Numeric, 0) = ?x both parse, load (installing the Type constraint on the variable), and FIRE by reading the carried type (subsort/provides discharged; suspend when under-determined, never NAF-decided); cargo-test green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-292"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-29T12:39:09Z"))

